Developing scalable web applications demands a clear separation of concerns, defensive programming, and rigorous data consistency across the stack.

### 1. Unified TypeScript Contracts
By declaring shared schema interfaces for requests and responses, frontend React components and Express controllers share a single source of truth. This prevents silent drift between client payloads and server models.

### 2. Authentication Beyond Cookies
While HTTP-only cookies protect against XSS token harvesting, Bearer tokens inside authorization headers provide seamless cross-domain support and microservice forwarding. Using standard JWT with tight expiration periods and refresh strategies balances usability and security.

### 3. Cascading Cleanups in NoSQL
MongoDB provides remarkable flexibility, but document relationships require deliberate lifecycle management. When deleting parent records such as blog posts, always ensure associated child records (like comments or attachments) are removed synchronously or through pre-delete hooks.

```javascript
// Cascading comment deletion example
postSchema.pre('findOneAndDelete', async function(next) {
  const doc = await this.model.findOne(this.getQuery());
  if (doc) {
    await Comment.deleteMany({ post: doc._id });
  }
  next();
});
```

With careful planning, the MERN stack delivers an unparalleled developer velocity and exceptional user experience.
